From: Amazing A32 kernel bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] prctl: initialize PR_SET_MM_AUXV stack buffer

GCC 11 can see the partially populated user_auxv array through the hardened
usercopy checks and reports a maybe-uninitialized warning. The MediaTek tree
builds kernel/ with -Werror, so that warning stops the build.

Initialize the array to zero. Newer upstream kernels use the same initialized
form, and this preserves the existing PR_SET_MM_AUXV copy length semantics.

--- a/kernel/sys.c
+++ b/kernel/sys.c
@@ -1915,7 +1915,7 @@ static int prctl_set_auxv(struct mm_struct *mm, unsigned long addr,
 	 * up to the caller to provide sane values here, otherwise userspace
 	 * tools which use this vector might be unhappy.
 	 */
-	unsigned long user_auxv[AT_VECTOR_SIZE];
+	unsigned long user_auxv[AT_VECTOR_SIZE] = {};
 
 	if (len > sizeof(user_auxv))
 		return -EINVAL;
